{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Entries now get a word count computed and stored on save, exposed as `word_count` in the API entry object. Build and existing unit/integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself is not covered by any test I ran.\n\n- **Migration**: adds a nullable `entries.word_count int` column. Existing entries are left null (no backfill).\n- **Counting**: whitespace-separated words of the entry content after `sanitizer.StripTags`, done in `internal/storage/entry.go` (`countEntryWords`).\n- **Writes**: `createEntry`, `updateEntry` and `UpdateEntryTitleAndContent` all write the count, so an existing entry gets populated the next time it is refreshed or its content is edited.\n- **Reads**: `model.Entry` gains `WordCount *int` (`json:\"word_count\"`), read in `fetchEntries`, so it serialises as null where unknown.\n\nThings you might not expect:\n- `internal/storage` now imports `internal/reader/sanitizer`.\n- `countEntryWords` has no `@effects` tag, because `StripTags` itself is untagged.\n- The Go `client` package's `Entry` struct was not updated with the new field.", "t": 1794463599.602}
